[the blueprints and every parameter, printed]
    V1 DOUBLE-GRID(g, R) [MINTS-FIRST, PHASE-SEPARATED]: 2g groups (g rows + g columns) on g^2 actors, 2g independent base lineages minted once (2 events each) and spread by 2g(g-1) bootstrap deliveries; then each round is 2g^2 proposals + g ROW arbitrations + g COLUMN arbitrations and ZERO deliveries.  At g = 4: 16 actors, 8 groups, k = 4 proposers per arbitration, 40 bootstrap events (8 mints, 24 deliveries) and 40 events per round.
    V2 SHARED-BASE(g): one lineage, spread to every actor, rows and columns conflicting on THAT base.  Built until it breaks; the break is gated against `prop_options_in_view` itself.
    V3 CONFLICT-GRID(g, R) [ROTATION]: D66's committed rotating blueprint — rounds alternate ROW and COLUMN groups on one lineage per actor, g - 1 deliveries per group per round.
    V4 DOUBLE-GRID(g, R, order='inter'): V1 with the arbitration order interleaved (row 0, col 0, row 1, col 1, ...).  Same events, same groups, same bootstrap; ONLY the arbitration order differs.
    ARBCHAIN*(m, k): one k-proposer arbitration, m k-proposer arbitration consumers and k - m delivery consumers, so the refined bound predicts |D_e(2)| = k*m + 2*(k - m) over [2k, k^2].
    SKY-B depths measured = (2, 3); committed SKYB_DEPTH = 2.  Full-menu replay budgets: 240s per record, 150s for the headline.
