    V2 SHARED-BASE(4): REFUSAL = ('COLUMN proposal by S01 ON THE SAME BASE', 18).  At that prefix (18 events: 1 mint + 15 deliveries + 1 proposal) the actor S01 holds the single lineage and already has a LIVE proposal on it.
      the layer's own option list `prop_options_in_view(view, S01)` = [] — EMPTY, because d42b1 skips a base on which the actor already has a live proposal; live triples in view = [('S01', ('v', ('v', 'v0'), (0,), ('S00',), 'S00'), 1)]; the whole menu offered to S01 has kinds ['n', 'r'] and contains NO proposal at all.
      MECHANISM, stated: a k-proposer conflict needs k live proposals ON ONE BASE, and one actor may hold AT MOST ONE live proposal per base.  A 4 x 4 grid whose rows and columns conflict CONCURRENTLY therefore needs TWO distinct unsuperseded bases per actor — i.e. 2g independent lineages — which is exactly what V1's mints-first bootstrap builds and why it cannot be replaced by a single mint-and-spread.
