[K1c THE CONFLICT BUDGET AT k = 4 — how much of a record CAN be arbitration?  (pin: 'the budget bound gives <= 1/5 for conflict groups at k = 4')]
  BOUND (D66's counting theorem of the layer, re-run here, not re-derived).  An
  arbitration's ckey is a set of k live proposal triples and a proposal is
  resolved by at most one arbitration in any record, so #proposals >= k * #arbs
  and the arbitration share of a record is at most 1/(k+1) with k the smallest
  proposer count in it.  Deliveries only lower it.  The step D66's round-1
  MINOR 3 supplied: two arbitrations consuming the same proposal triple share
  that proposer's register, `event_poset` makes them causally COMPARABLE, and
  the later one's View has the triple in `resolved` — so `admissible` refuses it.
    DOUBLE-GRID(g=4,R=1)             n=  80 arbs= 16 (k_min=1, k_conflict=4) arb share 1/5 (~0.2000) vs 1/(k_min+1) = 1/2; = 1/(k_conflict+1) = 1/5   <== THE CONFLICT GROUPS SATURATE
    DOUBLE-GRID(g=4,R=2)             n= 120 arbs= 24 (k_min=1, k_conflict=4) arb share 1/5 (~0.2000) vs 1/(k_min+1) = 1/2; = 1/(k_conflict+1) = 1/5   <== THE CONFLICT GROUPS SATURATE
    DOUBLE-GRID(g=4,R=3)             n= 160 arbs= 32 (k_min=1, k_conflict=4) arb share 1/5 (~0.2000) vs 1/(k_min+1) = 1/2; = 1/(k_conflict+1) = 1/5   <== THE CONFLICT GROUPS SATURATE
    DOUBLE-GRID(g=3,R=2)             n=  72 arbs= 18 (k_min=1, k_conflict=3) arb share 1/4 (~0.2500) vs 1/(k_min+1) = 1/2; = 1/(k_conflict+1) = 1/4   <== THE CONFLICT GROUPS SATURATE
    DOUBLE-GRID(g=3,R=4)             n= 120 arbs= 30 (k_min=1, k_conflict=3) arb share 1/4 (~0.2500) vs 1/(k_min+1) = 1/2; = 1/(k_conflict+1) = 1/4   <== THE CONFLICT GROUPS SATURATE
    DGRID-INTERLEAVED(g=3,R=2)       n=  72 arbs= 18 (k_min=1, k_conflict=3) arb share 1/4 (~0.2500) vs 1/(k_min+1) = 1/2; = 1/(k_conflict+1) = 1/4   <== THE CONFLICT GROUPS SATURATE
    DGRID-INTERLEAVED(g=4,R=2)       n= 120 arbs= 24 (k_min=1, k_conflict=4) arb share 1/5 (~0.2000) vs 1/(k_min+1) = 1/2; = 1/(k_conflict+1) = 1/5   <== THE CONFLICT GROUPS SATURATE
    CONFLICT-GRID(g=4,R=4)           n= 116 arbs= 16 (k_min=4, k_conflict=4) arb share 4/29 (~0.1379) vs 1/(k_min+1) = 1/5
    CONFLICT-GRID(g=4,R=6)           n= 180 arbs= 24 (k_min=4, k_conflict=4) arb share 2/15 (~0.1333) vs 1/(k_min+1) = 1/5
    THE k = 4 READING.  The DOUBLE-GRIDs mint their 2g base lineages with SINGLE-proposer arbitrations in the bootstrap, so k_min = 1 and the only GENERAL bound is 1/2 — but every conflict group of the g = 4 records has k = 4 and the measured share is EXACTLY 1/(4+1) = 1/5 = 1/5: the rounds saturate the conflict bound and the bootstrap spends none of the slack.  Records whose share equals 1/(k_conflict+1): ['DOUBLE-GRID(g=4,R=1)', 'DOUBLE-GRID(g=4,R=2)', 'DOUBLE-GRID(g=4,R=3)', 'DOUBLE-GRID(g=3,R=2)', 'DOUBLE-GRID(g=3,R=4)', 'DGRID-INTERLEAVED(g=3,R=2)', 'DGRID-INTERLEAVED(g=4,R=2)'].
