[K2b THE BRANCHING BOUNDS AT k = 4 — W4b with each record's OWN measured B, W4c with its OWN measured live Bl, and the refined depth-2 bound with THE RECORD'S OWN MEASURED k*b (pin K2)]
  W4b (D63): if every event carries at most B registers then |D_e(d)| <= B^d.
  W4c (D66, PROVED there from the committed layer): the version register an
  arbitration mints is a BIRTH WIRE with no P-successor, so |D_e(d)| <= Bl^d with
  Bl the maximum LIVE out-degree, and for an arbitration b <= #proposers = |regs| - 1.
  THE DEPTH-2 REFINEMENT (D66 BLOCKER 1): the EXACT containment D_e(2) SUBSET
  succ(e) u U{succ(y) : y in succ(e)} holds always; where no P-edge out of e skips
  a height layer it sharpens to |D_e(2)| <= SUM_y b(y) <= b(e)*Bl <= k*Bl <= k^2.
