    THE MECHANISM, MEASURED RATHER THAN GUESSED: the pin's lean was that the budget bound 1/(k+1) thins conflicts as k grows.  The k = 4 conflict share IS 1/5 against k = 3's 1/4 (K1c), and the width histograms of K3 show WHERE the homogeneity goes: the k = 4 records carry a large population of width-0 and width-1 charts (the bootstrap deliveries and the round's proposals) against a handful of very wide ones.  A wider record at fixed round count is a MORE heterogeneous record.
    THE ANSWER HAS TWO HALVES AND BOTH ARE STATED.  On the WHOLE record, no k = 4 record is in band at either depth: in-band-AND-sprinkling-grade-wide = d2 [], d3 [].  Under D60's OWN INTERIOR EXCISION — the control D66 used to answer its own residue 2, applied here to every record at both depths (K2c) — in-band-AND-wide = d2 [], d3 ['DOUBLE-GRID(g=4,R=2)'].
  [PASS] K4 [THE BAND VERDICT] **UNIFORMITY DOES NOT SURVIVE THE WIDTH AT k = 4 ON THE WHOLE RECORD — BUT IT DOES ON THE INTERIOR.**  The two halves, both measured, neither elided.  (i) NO swept k = 4 record is inside the recomputed sprinkling homogeneity band at either depth, so the pin's honest lean is CONFIRMED for whole records: k = 3 buys 9 directions and d = 3 band membership together (D66's flagship, re-run here at 47/60), k = 4 buys 16 and is out of band at both depths at every R this receipt could afford.  (ii) Under D60's OWN interior excision — the control D66 used to ANSWER its own residue 2, run here on every record at both depths — DOUBLE-GRID(4, 2) moves INTO the d = 3 band (0.5417 -> 0.7500) while its max |D| is unchanged at 16, so the campaign's first sprinkling-grade-wide-AND-in-band object exists at the SAME grade of evidence at which D66 closed its residue 2, and the shortfall of the whole record is to that extent an ENDS effect.  What does NOT happen at k = 4 is what happened at k = 3: no WHOLE k = 4 record is in band.  The predicate is band membership computed against the RE-RUN sprinkling band, with the interior control beside it.  THE NEGATIVE IS NOT AN ARTEFACT OF A MIS-SET BAND, and the gate says so: the SAME pipeline, the SAME re-run band and the SAME depth put D66's committed k = 3 flagship DOUBLE-GRID(3, 4) INSIDE the d = 3 band while it carries max |D| = 9 — so the instrument demonstrably CAN detect 'in-band and wide' where it exists, and the k = 4 rows are a measurement rather than a blind spot  (k = 4 records = 6; in band at d = 2 = 0, at d = 3 = 0; in band AND at/above the sprinkling width floor = d2 [] d3 []; the SAME on the INTERIOR = d2 [] d3 ['DOUBLE-GRID(g=4,R=2)']; the g = 3 anchor DOUBLE-GRID(3,4) is at d = 3 homogeneity 47/60 [IN ] with max |D| = 9)

[K5 THE COBOUNDARY GATE — D64's C7, BOTH ROUTES, at five port conventions, plus the convention-comparable PARITY route and the FREE-RELABELLING route.  The gauge question rides along at zero marginal cost and the pin declares NO LEAN either way]
